            <ArticleTitle>Obesity and breast cancer: role of inflammation and aromatase.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>T51-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1530/JME-13-0217</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Obesity is now recognised to be an inflammatory condition in which dysregulated metabolism plays an integral role. Inflammatory mediators regulate aromatase expression in the human breast as one mechanism whereby they increase the risk of breast cancer, especially in women who are obese.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
